## Solution

The matrix $M$ is **upper triangular** (all entries below the diagonal are zero). For an upper triangular matrix with nonzero diagonal entries, the inverse $M^{-1}$ is also upper triangular, and its **diagonal entries are the reciprocals** of the diagonal entries of $M$.

We are asked to find $\left(\frac{1}{839}M\right)^{-1}$ and compute its trace.

$$\left(\frac{1}{839}M\right)^{-1} = 839\,M^{-1}$$

$$\operatorname{tr}\!\left(839\,M^{-1}\right) = 839\,\operatorname{tr}\!\left(M^{-1}\right)$$

The diagonal of $M$ is:
$$23,\ -9,\ -16,\ 23,\ -10,\ -28,\ 27,\ 17,\ -33,\ -11,\ 6,\ 29$$

Therefore:
$$\operatorname{tr}(M^{-1}) = \frac{1}{23} - \frac{1}{9} - \frac{1}{16} + \frac{1}{23} - \frac{1}{10} - \frac{1}{28} + \frac{1}{27} + \frac{1}{17} - \frac{1}{33} - \frac{1}{11} + \frac{1}{6} + \frac{1}{29}$$

$$= \frac{2}{23} - \frac{1}{9} - \frac{1}{16} - \frac{1}{10} - \frac{1}{28} + \frac{1}{27} + \frac{1}{17} - \frac{1}{33} - \frac{1}{11} + \frac{1}{6} + \frac{1}{29}$$

Now multiply each term by $839$:

| Term | $839 \times$ term |
|------|-------------------|
| $2/23$ | $1678/23 \approx 72.9565$ |
| $-1/9$ | $-839/9 \approx -93.2222$ |
| $-1/16$ | $-839/16 = -52.4375$ |
| $-1/10$ | $-83.9$ |
| $-1/28$ | $-839/28 \approx -29.9643$ |
| $1/27$ | $839/27 \approx 31.0741$ |
| $1/17$ | $839/17 \approx 49.3529$ |
| $-1/33$ | $-839/33 \approx -25.4242$ |
| $-1/11$ | $-839/11 \approx -76.2727$ |
| $1/6$ | $839/6 \approx 139.8333$ |
| $1/29$ | $839/29 \approx 28.9310$ |

Summing column by column:

$$72.9565 - 93.2222 - 52.4375 - 83.9 - 29.9643 + 31.0741 + 49.3529 - 25.4242 - 76.2727 + 139.8333 + 28.9310$$

$$\approx -39.0731$$

Rounding to the nearest integer:

$$\boxed{-39}$$

